        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0444" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg350"/>

                <head>No. 259.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vignaud to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 29, 1887</date>.
                        (Received September 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 472.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have communicated with Mr. Flourens with
                    reference to the subject-matter of your instruction of June 14, 1887, No. 235,
                    and under date of the 26th instant he writes that our commercial agent at Nouméa
                    has been misinformed, but that in view of complying more fully with your desire
                    the governors of New Caledonia and of Guiana have been instructed to abstain,
                    until further orders, from issuing authorization to liberated convicts to
                    proceed to the United States.</p>
                <p>I send herewith a copy and a translation of Mr. Flourens’s note.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Vignaud.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d259-a1.xml" xpointer="d259-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
